Why the two are mixed: a concurrent `git add -A` picked up in-progress files
from another session rather than scoping the commit to the paths that session
had touched. The repository's own CLAUDE.md warns about exactly this and asks
for path-scoped commits when several agents or a cron write to one checkout.

Nothing here is wrong or untested -- the feature landed complete, and its own
follow-up test is 797bd291. Only the history is misleading, and the commit was
already pushed when that was noticed, so it was left intact rather than
rewritten.

Read the feature as: this commit (minus the two files above) plus 797bd291.
Design rationale lives in docs/explanation/github-repository-ingestion.md,
section "Filing repositories starred somewhere else".
